course: dictionary
lesson: 9703
title: Sulfur: a yellow element with a rotten-egg smell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sulfur is a chemical element. An element is a pure substance made of only one kind of atom, and it cannot be split into anything simpler. Sulfur is a yellow non-metal, and its chemical symbol is S.
explain: Every element has an atomic number. Sulfur's is 16, which means every sulfur atom has 16 protons in its centre. Find the letter S on the periodic table and you will find sulfur.
explain: Context helps here too. «Volcanoes release gases such as water vapour, carbon dioxide and sulfur dioxide, and their sulfur gases can smell of rotten eggs.» The word sulfur sits next to gases and smell, so the clues tell you that sulfur gases are gases that contain sulfur, and that some of them smell like rotten eggs.
fact: Sulfur is a chemical element with the symbol S and atomic number 16.
fact: Sulfur is a yellow non-metal, often found as yellow crystals near volcanoes and hot springs.
fact: When sulfur burns, or forms some compounds, it gives off a smell like rotten eggs.
fact: Sulfur is used to make sulfuric acid, matches, rubber and fertilisers. In the UK it is also spelled sulphur.
fact: «Brimstone» is an old word for sulfur, as in «fire and brimstone» in the Bible.
exercise: What is the chemical symbol for sulfur? | *S | Sl | Sf | Su
exercise: «Volcanoes release gases such as water vapour, carbon dioxide and sulfur dioxide.» Which of these gases contains sulfur? | *Sulfur dioxide | Carbon dioxide | Steam | Water vapour
exercise: When sulfur burns, what kind of smell does it give off? | Cut grass | *Rotten eggs | Fresh roses | Ocean salt
test: Sulfur has an atomic number of what? | 6 | 14 | 18 | *16
test: Where might you find yellow sulfur crystals? | In tall trees | Deep inside ice | Inside the deep ocean | *Near volcanoes and hot springs
exam: Which statement about sulfur is correct? | Sulfur is a shiny silver metal | Sulfur is a liquid that is blue and cold | Sulfur is a gas that never burns | *Sulfur is a yellow non-metal with the symbol S, and some of its compounds smell like rotten eggs
